  "rules": [
    "Model forecasts exhibit a persistent upward bias during high-volatility regimes, consistently overestimating the peak of price spikes by approximately 3-5 EUR.",
    "The model fails to capture immediate mean reversion after sharp rallies; true outcomes often reverse direction within 2-4 days while the forecast continues linearly upward.",
    "Sentiment signals (0.50) appear to trigger a delayed reaction in the market, causing the model to overreact to sentiment by projecting further gains that are not realized until later or not at all.",
    "The forecast horizon is structurally flawed for this asset class, assuming a smooth trend where the true outcome is characterized by erratic, non-linear swings.",
    "Apply a downward correction of 4-6 EUR to the initial forecast value when the last 3 days show a spike followed by a sentiment shift or volatility increase."
  ]
}
